  "body": "## Governing chain\nAddendum to the single-source-of-truth deterministic mandate under Priority-1 UMR-20260806-171945-5767.\nReal gap: `superboss-register.sqlite` existed at 5 paths on the host, 4 of them 0-byte decoys that\nopened as a valid-but-empty SQLite DB instead of erroring -- a silent-wrong-answer trap.\n\nThis PR was produced across two invocations of `task-20260813-150119-remove-0-byte-decoy-register-files-that`\n(dispatched under UMR-20260813-130245-6a26). **Invocation 1 was a genuine stuck-task SIGKILL** (no exit\n60s after SIGTERM, likely the 4-parallel-subagent scan across the whole scripts tree exceeding the\nworker's stuck-task timeout) -- correctly killed by the supervisor, no dispatch-gateway bug. **Invocation 2**\n(resumed) did the real rewrite + decoy archival but stopped cleanly, mid-task, when its own session\nbudget ran out (~$0.98 of $10 left) before opening this PR. This RCA task (UMR-20260814-061712-f9b0)\nindependently re-verified the pushed commit, rebased it onto current `main` (was 77 commits behind,\nrebased clean, zero conflicts), re-ran `py_compile` on all 24 changed files + `bash -n` on the shell\nscript (all clean), completed item F below, and opens this PR.\n\n## What changed (real diff, 24 files + worker-entrypoint.sh)\nEvery real hazard site that resolved the Superboss Register DB path via a hardcoded literal, a\nself-built `os.path.join()`, or an independent re-read of `SUPERBOSS_REGISTER_DB` now delegates to\nthe one real canonical resolver, `superboss-register.py`'s `resolve_superboss_db_path()`\n(exists / non-zero-size / SQLite-magic-bytes / `umr_tasks`-table verification, hard-fails via\n`SuperbossDbPathError` on a decoy/corrupt file) -- via the same lazy-import-cached\n`_superboss_register()` / `_resolve_db_path()` convention already established in\n`reconcile_stale_running_workers.py` / `worker-exit-status-bridge.py`.\n\nFiles: automation_rule_engine.py, batch-import-conversation-log.py, context_engine.py,\ndirective_engine.py, generate_platform_completion_checklist.py, generate_wiring_registry.py\n(read-path only), health-check-15min.py, intent_engine.py, knowledge_registry_multisource.py,\nlearning_engine.py, metadata_reconciliation.py, migrate_2026-07-31_dedup_constraints.py,\nowner_status.py, plan_generator.py, prompt_gateway/gateway_persistence.py (read-path only),\nprune_memory_backups.py, regenerate_master_index.py, scripts/superboss_gateway.py,\nsecurity-check.py, task-gateway.py (2 direct-open read sites only), veridian-task-watchdog.py\n(2 sites), wiring_registry_zero_gap_audit.py, worker-entrypoint.sh, workflow_contract.py.\n\n`superboss-register.py` and `resource_governor.py` are untouched (narrow 2026-08-08 stop-work\norder; both are read-only reference points here, not widened).\n\n4 zero-byte decoy files on the host were independently found, verified unreferenced by any real\ncode path, and archived in place (`.empty-stub-superseded-2026-08-13` suffix, following this\nrepo's own 2026-07-29 precedent) -- none were git-tracked, so no repo diff results from that step.\n\n## Item F -- real proof-run (done this invocation)\nReal DB resolution:\n```\nresolve_superboss_db_path() -> /opt/veridian/ai-os/memory/superboss-register.sqlite\n```\nHard-fail on a genuine 0-byte scratch file:\n```\nresolve_superboss_db_path(default_path='/tmp/rca-6a26-zero-byte-scratch.sqlite')\n-> SuperbossDbPathError: Superboss Register DB path verification FAILED at check\n   'non-zero size' (known stale-decoy signature): path_checked='/tmp/rca-6a26-zero-byte-scratch.sqlite'\n   size_found=0\n```\nRewritten real caller (`owner_status.py`), run from a different cwd (`/var/tmp`), confirmed it\nstill resolves and reads the real 4.07GB DB and prints real rows.\n\n## Item D -- explicitly NOT resolved here, flagged for dedicated follow-up (not fabricated as done)\n`directive_engine.py`, `plan_generator.py`, `security-check.py`, `prompt_gateway/gateway_persistence.py`\neach wrap their DB call site in a pre-existing broad except-Exception (or narrower) fail-open\ncontract, predating this change and in each case documented in-file as deliberate (\"never block a\nreal, legitimate submission/read on a broken check\"). That wrapper will now also silently swallow\n`SuperbossDbPathError` -- i.e. if the DB ever again resolves to a decoy/corrupt file, these 4 call\nsites will fail open exactly as before, silently, rather than propagating the loud failure this PR\notherwise adds everywhere else. This is a real, judgment-requiring product decision (change the\ncontract for these 4 vs. leave it) that a rewrite-focused pass shouldn't silently resolve either way\nby guessing -- left untouched and explicitly called out here, same as the original invocation's own\nhonest disclosure, rather than being resolved under RCA time pressure.\n\n`health-check-15min.py`, `knowledge_registry_multisource.py`, `metadata_reconciliation.py`: removing\nthe old isfile pre-check means a missing DB now hard-fails/propagates instead of degrading\ngracefully -- an intended consequence of closing the hazard, flagged here for awareness, not yet\nindependently re-verified against each file's real callers/cron schedule.\n\n## RCA disposition of UMR-20260813-130245-6a26\nRecorded separately via `resource_governor.py mark-umr-terminal` citing this PR, in the RCA task's\nown progress doc (compliance-tracker, `progress/task-20260814-061732-rca--umr-20260813-130245-6a26-killed.md`).\n\nGenerated with Claude Code\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
